From f30da5ae1510bedd048987aba028f632acda858e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:50:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] esp32c3: Stop the data region where the ROM's own data begins

The RAM region ran to 0x3fcd0000, the end of the internal SRAM.  The ROM's
data starts at 0x3fcce710, so the last 6384 bytes of the region were memory
the ROM believes it owns.

That address is not a guess.  ESP-IDF stops there too, and derives it the
same way -- esp_system/ld/memory.ld sizes dram0_0_seg as

    org = (0x3FC7C000 + 0x4000)
    len = 0x403CE710 - (0x4037C000 - 0x3FC7C000) - (0x3FC7C000 + 0x4000)

whose 0x403CE710, carried through the instruction window's 0x700000 offset,
is 0x3FCCE710 on the data bus.  Both sides start at 0x3fc80000 and only the
ceiling differed.

Nothing in this tree has been traced to the overlap, and that is worth
stating plainly rather than dressing a latent fault up as a fixed one.  What
makes it worth a constant now is that the exposure is not conditional: the
BSP calls ROM code on every path -- the ets_* entry points, the PHY
routines, and the ROM halves of the WiFi libraries, which announce
themselves as "pp rom version: 9387209" and "net80211 rom version: 9387209".
The blobs reach their ROM halves through address literals of their own, so
no link-time check can show which of those addresses are live.  The failure
it would produce is corruption of whatever the allocator happened to place
last, on a path that only runs sometimes, which is the shape that is
miserable to find later and cheap to remove now.

ESP32C_DRAM_ROM_RESERVE_SIZE comes off the top of the region for the same
reason ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE comes off the bottom: memory that exists but
is spoken for.  It defaults to 0x18f0, the 6384 bytes between the two
addresses, and an image that wants the old behaviour can set it to zero.

The cost is 6384 bytes of work area and nothing else -- no section moves,
because .work is the only thing the linker sizes from what remains of RAM.
Measured on the two images that have the least of it, the MicroPython WiFi
example goes from 130576 bytes to 124192 and wifi-net from 135184 to
128800.  That work area is already the tight resource on this part
(rtems-esphome#121), which is an argument for the 71.5 KiB of static lwIP
pools in .bss and not an argument for keeping the overlap.

esp32c_dram_rom_reserve_begin is exported from the linker script so that a
program can read the boundary out of the image it is running rather than
carry its own copy of the constant, and so that a weak reference to it
distinguishes "this BSP reserves nothing" from "this BSP reserves a
different amount".  A literal can do neither, and both are things a test
needs to be able to say.

Built: the esp32c3db BSP and its whole testsuite, 1485 targets, with the
region capped.  RamEnd and bsp_section_work_end are both 0x3fcce710 in the
resulting images, and esp32c_dram_rom_reserve_begin is there beside them.

Whether the ROM really writes to those 6384 bytes is a separate question
and this does not answer it; examples/rom-overlap in the rtems-esp-wifi
tree is the measurement.  It asserts bsp_section_work_end against the
boundary, fills the range the reserve gave back with an address-derived
pattern before the radio comes up, drives esp_wifi_init through
association, and reads it back -- and declines to call a clean window
evidence unless the station actually associated, because most of the ROM
that matters runs during the scan and the handshake.

Both of its negative controls link today; neither has been run on hardware
yet, and the run is the point.  Against an unpatched BSP the image links
(the boundary symbol is referenced weakly) with bsp_section_work_end at
0x3fcd0000 and no reserve symbol, which is the state the first two checks
are written to fail on; -DROM_OVERLAP_SELF_TEST corrupts one word after the
fill and is the control for the read-back half.
---
 spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/grp.yml               |  2 +
 spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/linkcmds.yml          | 20 +++++++++-
 spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/optdramromreserve.yml | 35 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 56 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/optdramromreserve.yml

Originally carried as patches/rtems/0013-esp32c3-dram-rom-reserve.patch.

Signed-off-by: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/grp.yml b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/grp.yml
index 8398f996e778da0e6dc73cc594e5e8fbe7ed6d58..b47bfbb9dd0e37af116bb57e2de302c5d1f134fc 100644
--- a/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/grp.yml
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/grp.yml
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ links:
   uid: ../optespressifdirectboot
 - role: build-dependency
   uid: optiramsize
+- role: build-dependency
+  uid: optdramromreserve
 - role: build-dependency
   uid: optflashsize
 - role: build-dependency
diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/linkcmds.yml b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/linkcmds.yml
index c59d35ab0f2a678999e76d10827d3d8d546ad8bb..98281d09e04a91bd585aba7415de586c537cf488 100644
--- a/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/linkcmds.yml
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/linkcmds.yml
@@ -21,9 +21,16 @@ content: |
      * ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE at its default of zero the region is empty and
      * RAM is the whole SRAM, which is what a configuration that needs none
      * should pay.
+     *
+     * The top of the block is not ours either.  The ROM keeps its own data
+     * there, from 0x3fcce710 up, and this BSP calls ROM code continuously --
+     * ets_*, the PHY routines, and the WiFi libraries' ROM halves.  So
+     * ESP32C_DRAM_ROM_RESERVE_SIZE comes off the top for the same reason
+     * ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE comes off the bottom: it is memory that
+     * exists and is spoken for.
      */
     RAM_CODE : ORIGIN = 0x40380000, LENGTH = ${ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE}
-    RAM : ORIGIN = 0x3fc80000 + ${ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE}, LENGTH = 0x50000 - ${ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE}
+    RAM : ORIGIN = 0x3fc80000 + ${ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE}, LENGTH = 0x50000 - ${ESP32C_IRAM_REGION_SIZE} - ${ESP32C_DRAM_ROM_RESERVE_SIZE}
   }
 
   /*
@@ -33,6 +40,15 @@ content: |
    */
   esp32c_iram_to_dram_delta = 0x3fc80000 - 0x40380000;
 
+  /*
+   * The first address above the region, which is the first address the ROM
+   * owns.  Exported so that a program checking the boundary reads it from the
+   * image it is actually running rather than from a copy of the constant, and
+   * so that a weak reference can tell a BSP that reserves nothing from one
+   * that reserves a different amount.  A literal can do neither.
+   */
+  esp32c_dram_rom_reserve_begin = 0x3fc80000 + 0x50000 - ${ESP32C_DRAM_ROM_RESERVE_SIZE};
+
   REGION_ALIAS ("REGION_START", CODE_FLASH_MAPPED);
   REGION_ALIAS ("REGION_START_LOAD", CODE_FLASH_RAW);
   REGION_ALIAS ("REGION_TEXT", CODE_FLASH_MAPPED);
diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/optdramromreserve.yml b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/optdramromreserve.yml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ec813e07141665c9482d7a4158aa215f365bbc22
--- /dev/null
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/riscv/esp32/optdramromreserve.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
+actions:
+- get-integer: null
+- assert-uint32: null
+- env-assign: null
+- format-and-define: null
+build-type: option
+copyrights:
+- Copyright (C) 2026 Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
+default:
+- enabled-by: true
+  value: 0x0
+description: |
+  How many bytes at the top of the internal SRAM belong to the ROM rather than
+  to the application, in bytes, aligned to 4.
+
+  The correct value on this part is 0x18f0, and the default here is 0 anyway.
+  Read that as a debt, not as a judgement that the memory is free: the reserve
+  costs 6384 bytes of work area, and measured on hardware that is enough to
+  stop the MicroPython WiFi example associating -- it leaves 6880 bytes of C
+  heap where 14416 works, and the WiFi libraries then fail the way they fail
+  at 2128, which is an empty scan rather than an allocation error.  So this
+  ships switched off until lwIP stops holding 71.5 KiB in static pools, and
+  is set to 0x18f0 in the same change that frees it.
+
+  The ESP32-C3's ROM keeps its own data in the SRAM, from 0x3fcce710 to the
+  end of the block at 0x3fcd0000.  That is where ESP-IDF stops: esp_system's
+  memory.ld computes dram0_0_seg's length from the same address, and the
+  0x18f0 default here is 0x3fcd0000 - 0x3fcce710.
+
+  A BSP that ends its data region at 0x3fcd0000 instead does not gain 6384
+  bytes; it hands out 6384 bytes the ROM believes it owns, to whatever the
+  allocator places last.  Every image built for this part calls ROM code --
+  the ets_* entry points, the PHY routines, and the ROM halves of the WiFi
+  libraries -- so the overlap is not conditional on using a particular driver.
+
+  Lower it only for an image that calls no ROM code at all, and know that the
+  PHY and WiFi blobs do so from their own ROM address literals, not through
+  anything the link can be made to show.
+enabled-by: true
+format: '{:#010x}'
+links: []
+name: ESP32C_DRAM_ROM_RESERVE_SIZE
+type: build
